# Runtime crawl output — contains other people's website content. Never commit.
work/

# Internal design notes. Not published.
#
# dev-notes/ names real client sites and describes the structured-data defects
# found on them, which is exactly what makes it useful while building and
# exactly what must not become public. It stays on the private remote.
#
# Source comments and docs/dev/ cite it as `dev-notes/NN` — those are citations
# to an archive you may not have, not broken links. The substance is always in
# the comment itself.
dev-notes/

# The corpus target list. Client hostnames, one per line.
sites.txt
sites.txt~

# Local agent configuration. Also covered by most users' global gitignore, but
# not everyone has one, and this file records paths and hostnames from whatever
# was last worked on.
#
# Deliberately this one file and NOT `.claude/`. That directory is mixed rather
# than private: `settings.json`, `agents/`, `commands/`, `skills/` and `hooks/`
# are all project configuration meant to be shared. Ignoring the directory would
# silently drop anything added there later — the file would simply never appear
# in the repository, with nothing to say so.
.claude/settings.local.json

node_modules/
dist/
*.log

.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*~
